      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WRITTEN DOLL (1) returned for his second campaign with a sound on-pace third over today's journey at Kembla Grange. Tongue-tie goes on from the good draw with the key jockey change. Hard to hold out. ANDARNA (7) started hard in the market on resumption with a fast-finishing second from back in the field over 1000m at Kembla Grange. Tommy Berry retains the mount and she looks ready for the 1200m. Leading contender. DAME DIVIDEND (8) seven weeks between runs when taken back from the wide gate before launching late with a tough third over 1250m at Newcastle. Finds a suitable race from a much better draw. Can box seat and figure prominently. ANTHROPOID (2) back for his third prep and gelded over the break. Raced in Group company last time in and returns with the two trials under his belt. Winkers come off and must be respected.",
